        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Now you teach each other. Listen carefully; you will be tested on all six.' Time each expert at 2 minutes (call 'Switch'). Circulate and listen for accuracy. Pose the whole-group question: 'Which organisms in our river benefit from the changes, and which do not?' WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds. Cold-call 5 learners from different groups to share claims and ask 'What evidence from the reading supports that?' Address misconceptions: 'Adaptations are not chosen by the organism; they arise over generations through natural selection.' Clarify that the unpleasant smell and the weeds are signs of an environment changing, and that we still need to find out why (next lessons).",
